.TH STAMP 1ptk "November 2026" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
detab \- convert tabs to spaces and remove whitespace at the end of lines.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/bin/detab
[
.I -hv
]
.I pattern ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B detab
processes from standard input to standard output
converting tabs to spaces and removing whitespace
at the end of lines.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Increase verbosity.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
.B detab < file0 > file1
.EE
Convert tabs and remove trailing whitespace from
.B file0 ,
saving resulting text into
.B file1 .
.SH AUTHORS
Paul Kinney.
